Bundled data (shipped in this repository)
-----------------------------------------
- Cancer incidence figures in `src/pmhc_triage/data/burden_bundle.csv`
  Source: Global Cancer Observatory, Cancer Today (2024 estimates), International
  Agency for Research on Cancer / WHO. https://gco.iarc.who.int/today
  These are a small set of individual, cited incidence figures (World and country
  proxies for Europe/EastAsia/SouthAsia = Germany/China/India), included as cited
  reference facts — not a reproduction of the GLOBOCAN database. © IARC/WHO;
  reused with attribution for research use. Refine per-region for a real analysis.

- Derived validation results in `validation/*.json`, `validation/*.png`
  Aggregate results (coverage fractions, effective-N estimates, calibration ratios)
  computed by this tool from the sources below. Facts/derived statistics, cited.

NOT bundled (fetched or supplied at the user's request)
-------------------------------------------------------
- HLA allele frequencies: Allele Frequency Net Database (AFND), CC BY-NC.
  http://www.allelefrequencies.net  — deliberately NOT redistributed. `pmhc-triage
  fetch-freqs` retrieves them on the user's machine under the user's own AFND terms.
- Antigen frequencies: cBioPortal (ODbL). https://www.cbioportal.org  — queried live;
  some studies carry additional non-commercial restrictions (check per study).

Referenced sources (queried at runtime; not redistributed)
----------------------------------------------------------
- UniProt (CC BY 4.0) · Open Targets: data CC0, code Apache-2.0 ·
  MHCflurry (Apache-2.0) · IHME GBD (per IHME terms).

Literature
----------
- Marty et al. 2017, Cell 171:1272-1283 (immunoediting / PHBR). Derived summary
  statistics only (open supplement), cited in `validation/`.
- Bui et al. 2006, Immunogenetics (HLA population-coverage method).
